      <memberdef kind="function" id="class_a_g_remap_core_1_1_tex_thumbprint_1a61bba32d7ce38368e712de441338d898" prot="public" static="yes" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>std::optional&lt; std::vector&lt; double &gt; &gt;</type>
        <definition>std::optional&lt; std::vector&lt; double &gt; &gt; AGRemapCore::TexThumbprint::of</definition>
        <argsstring>(const std::string &amp;path, int size)</argsstring>
        <name>of</name>
        <qualifiedname>AGRemapCore::TexThumbprint::of</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>const std::string &amp;</type>
          <declname>path</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>int</type>
          <declname>size</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
The thumbprint of the image at &apos;path&apos;: an ``size`` x ``size`` grid, row-major, of the
mean of each block&apos;s ``(r + g + b) / 3``, rounded :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;`
:raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;`

Blocks are ``(width / size)`` x ``(height / size)`` and the remainder is dropped, so an
image whose sides do not divide evenly is thumbprinted from its top-left. Alpha is not
read at all
</verbatim></para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>path</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The image to read </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>size</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The grid&apos;s side <ndash/> the thumbprint holds &apos;size&apos; * &apos;size&apos; values</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>The thumbprint, or <computeroutput>std::nullopt</computeroutput> if the file will not open, holds no image, or is smaller than &apos;size&apos; on either side </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="include/AGRemapCore/model/textures/TexThumbprint.h" line="77" column="34" bodyfile="src/model/textures/TexThumbprint.cpp" bodystart="25" bodyend="64"/>
